# Shared app code

Use `lib/` for general app code reused across views, components, or backend functions, such as helpers, constants, types, and validation schemas. Import modules with `#lib/...`, for example `import { formatName } from "#lib/format-name"`.

This folder is a recommended convention; Patchsmith does not enforce it or automatically register its files. Keep code specific to one feature beside that feature until it needs to be shared.

Modules used by both frontend and backend should work in both runtimes. Keep database access and server-only dependencies in backend modules, and UI dependencies in frontend modules.
